---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Sessions 19&ndash;20: CAM Programming</h1>
        <p class="text-sn-theme">The Arcade Cabinet Project &mdash; Milestone 3 of 5</p>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <h2>Nothing New to Learn Here</h2>
          <p>
            Every skill this milestone needs already exists from Weeks
            3&ndash;4: toolpath types, offset, pocket/step-over,
            step-down, tabs, sequencing, and your own pre-cut checklist.
          </p>

          <p>
            The difference is scale &mdash; your real cabinet has several
            panels, not one small test coupon. Each one needs its own job,
            programmed with the same discipline Session 9 and Session 12
            already established.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Bungee cords aren't part of this
            project</b> &mdash; but every CNC safety protocol from Session 4
            still applies to every panel you program and every test cut you
            run.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <h3>Step 1: List Every Panel That Needs a CAM Job</h3>
          <p>
            Go through your Milestone 2 assembly and list every distinct
            flat panel that will be CNC-cut. Note which toolpath types
            (profile, pocket, drill) each one actually needs &mdash; not
            every panel needs all three.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Check every hole's diameter against
            your available bits before you decide it's a drill.</b> This is
            where Session 7's catch bites for real: your button and joystick
            cutouts are far larger than any bit in the shop, so those are
            pockets or interior profiles, not drills. Getting this wrong here
            means discovering it at the machine in Milestone 4.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 2: Program Each Panel's Job</h3>
          <p>
            For each panel, set up a CAM Studio job: pocket and drill
            operations first, profile cut last, with tabs. Use Outside
            offset for panels being cut free, Inside for any interior
            holes cut to exact size.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 3: Simulate Every Job</h3>
          <p>
            Run the simulation for each panel individually. Confirm
            sequencing, offsets, and step-over/step-down choices before
            moving to the next panel.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 4: Run Your Pre-Cut Checklist, Per Panel</h3>
          <p>
            Apply your Session 10 checklist to each panel's job
            individually &mdash; a checklist run once for the whole project
            isn't the same as checking each actual job.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Before Milestone 4 begins, confirm for every panel:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Toolpath order is pocket/drill, then profile</li>
            <li>Offset choice is justified for that specific panel</li>
            <li>Tabs are included wherever a profile cut fully separates the part</li>
            <li>Your pre-cut checklist has been run against that panel's actual job</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these on your own. Reflections are individual, even when the rest of the session was team work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>Did programming multiple real panels change how you think about the pre-cut checklist, compared to applying it to just Sessions 12&ndash;13's single practice piece?</li>
            <li>Milestone 4 is fabrication, and there is one router for the whole class. Which panel will your team cut first, and why that one before the others?</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Submit your CAM Studio files for every panel, your per-panel
            checklist run-throughs, and your reflection.
          </p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Milestone Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
